// LoyaltyPlus — a "+N: [effect]" loyalty ability [CR#606.2,606.4]: paying a
// "+" loyalty cost puts that many loyalty counters on the permanent. Loyalty
// abilities follow special activation rules [CR#606.3,306.5d]: sorcery speed
// only (`window: SorcerySpeed`), and SHARED across every loyalty ability of
// the permanent, not per-ability — `limits: [LoyaltyOncePerTurn]` is that
// shared gate (`GameState::can_activate`'s `LoyaltyOncePerTurn` arm finds a
// permanent's OTHER loyalty abilities by cost shape, no dedicated ability
// tag). Macros can't branch on a param's sign ([macros-declarative-not-
// programming]), so the "+"/"−"/"0" cost verb is chosen by macro NAME
// (mirrors `LoyaltyMinus`/`LoyaltyZero`), not by a signed-number param —
// the author writes `LoyaltyPlus(n: 1, effect: …)` for "[+1]: …".
//
// Usage: LoyaltyPlus(n: 1, effect: <effect>).
(
    name: "LoyaltyPlus",
    template: "+${n}: ${effect}",
    kinds: [Ability],
    params: { "n": Count, "effect": OneShotEffect },
    body: Activated(
        cost: [Do(PutCounters(This, LoyaltyCounter, Param(n)))],
        window: SorcerySpeed,
        limits: [LoyaltyOncePerTurn],
        effect: Param(effect),
    ),
)
